load:
warning: $STARTER/deny-list-exec/agent.yaml:5:34: deny_read: [] disables the built-in list (~/.ssh, ~/.aws, ~/.netrc, ~/.gnupg, npm/git/gh/docker/kube/gcloud credentials, browser profiles, .env files) [deny-read-disabled]
  fix: remove deny_read: to keep the built-in list
compile:
warning: $STARTER/deny-list-exec/agent.yaml:6:7: command rules read every image's #! line: at tier landlock, run unprivileged, the supervisor reads as the agent's user, so every exec of an image that user cannot read (an execute-only file, such as RHEL's sudo, mode 4111) is refused image-unreadable with EACCES, even an image no rule names (ADR 0048 R13); a supervisor running as root (sudo tego run, tiers cgroup and bpflsm) reads every image on a local file system, but an NFS export with root_squash serves it as the anonymous user and a FUSE mount without allow_other or allow_root refuses it [exec-rule-coverage]
  fix: make such images readable by the agent's user, or run at a root tier
warning: $STARTER/deny-list-exec/agent.yaml:6:7: exec: is a deny-list beside fs.write: the agent can write files and run them; a copy of git under another name is not git to these rules, and neither is a copy run from a memfd or from a file it deleted [exec-rule-coverage]
  fix: restrict images with exec.allow (and a plane tier for native code under write entries, ADR 0027)
warning: $STARTER/deny-list-exec/agent.yaml:6:7: best effort (exec.rules/argv): argv is copied unless the decision plane pins the run's execs (where doctor's exec pin cell, plane.exec_pin, passed in the plane's mode); on the fanotify fallback an allow is a copied fact; a refusal is exact, an allow is recorded in run_start best_effort and never counted as enforced (ADR 0048 (6)) [unenforced]
  fix: bound effects with fs and net rules: command rules are launch rules
warning: $STARTER/deny-list-exec/agent.yaml:6:7: best effort (exec.rules/argv): argv is copied unless the plane pins the run's execs (where doctor's exec pin cell, plane.exec_pin, passed in the plane's mode); a refusal is exact, an allow is recorded in run_start best_effort and never counted as enforced (ADR 0048 (6)) [unenforced]
  fix: bound effects with fs and net rules: command rules are launch rules
warning: $STARTER/deny-list-exec/agent.yaml:6:7: best effort (exec.rules/argv): argv is copied: the supervisor decides on its copy, and the kernel copies argv again after an allow; a refusal is exact, an allow is recorded in run_start best_effort and never counted as enforced (ADR 0048 (6)) [unenforced]
  fix: bound effects with fs and net rules: command rules are launch rules
